<article class="env-definition" id="03X0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03X0">Definition <span data-tag="03X0">34.5.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathit{Sch}_{smooth}$ be a big smooth site containing $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>big smooth site of $S$</em>, denoted $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{smooth}$, is the site $\mathit{Sch}_{smooth}/S$ introduced in Sites, Section <a href="/tag/00XZ" data-tag="00XZ">7.25</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>big affine smooth site of $S$</em>, denoted $(\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth}$, is the full subcategory of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{smooth}$ whose objects are affine $U/S$. A covering of $(\textit{Aff}/S)_{smooth}$ is any covering $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{smooth}$ which is a standard smooth covering. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>